// MiraVelo bike leasing: the real parts of this example and how we source them.
// Read it top-down: Customer, Back office and Operations at the top, commodities at the bottom right.
// Decorators: build = Make, buy = Buy a product, outsource = Buy as a service, market = Partner.
// No decorator = open decision. Annotations 1 to 3 name the open decisions, GitHub issues #8 to #10.
// Annotation 4: the credit check is a human decision in the inbox today; #19 automates it with the DMN.
// Back-office task UI was decided as build (ADR-0010, issue #11): the own inbox in the frontend.
// Adapt has no decorator of its own: it is buy plus an "Adapt" annotation. No component is adapted today.
// Insurance policy as a partner and Database outsource (managed PostgreSQL) are assumptions.
// Products: Process engine = CIB seven, Process monitoring = CIB seven Cockpit,
// Application framework = Spring Boot, UI framework = React and Vite, Database = PostgreSQL.
// Notes: green = Doctrine (talk colour legend); the uncoloured notes mark decisions and assumptions.
// Rationale, BPMN element ids and code per component: sourcing-decisions.md next to this file.
